			"notes": "The wait is over: a version of PlusTiC is finally available for a newer version of Minecraft!\n\nThis release is a very early build, and it includes only a small set of features for testing purposes.  More features will be ported in the future; this release is intended to collect user feedback.\n\nIn this version, the \"Gems\" and \"GemsPlus\" modules were added, which includes support for the gems introduced by Project Red and GemsPlusPlus.  (Note: in the original PlusTiC, these modules also included support for certain gems added in Biomes o' Plenty; the gems had been removed from Biomes o' Plenty, so they were not ported over.)\n\nKnown Issues:\n- Most of the modifiers (traits) have been implemented only in name, but the effects have not been ported.\n- The handle material stats are not yet balanced, as Tinkers' Construct 3 changed the stats system. (Help wanted!)\n- The textures of materials have a low contrast, making the edges hard to see"
		}
